.TH IAD\-TEXT\-VIEW 3 "" "iced-adaptive-design 0.1.0" "iced-adaptive-design Manual"
.SH NAME
text_view \- a multi\-line editor over a text_editor::Content
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
text_view(content: &'a text_editor::Content)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBGtkTextView\fR: a multi\-line editor over a \fBtext_editor::Content\fR. Without \fBon_action\fR it is read\-only and drawn disabled.
.PP
\fBFixed or growing.\fR By default it is a fixed \fBheight\fR and scrolls. Give it a maximum, \fBmax_lines\fR or \fBmax_height\fR, and it becomes a textarea that \fBgrows with its text\fR from \fBmin_lines\fR (default one line) up to that maximum, then scrolls. Without a maximum it never grows: an unbounded textarea would push the rest of the page away without limit.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B text_view(content: &'a text_editor::Content)
.SH PROPERTIES
Builder methods, chained after the constructor.
.TP
.B \&.placeholder(p: impl Into<String>)
.TP
.B \&.single_line(enabled: bool)
Keep input to a single line: ignore Enter and normalize pasted line breaks to spaces.
.TP
.B \&.height(h: impl Into<Length>)
The fixed height of a view that does not grow (default 90). Ignored once a maximum is set.
.TP
.B \&.min_lines(lines: usize)
The fewest lines a growing view shows, however short its text (default 1). Only applies with a maximum.
.TP
.B \&.max_lines(lines: usize)
Makes the view grow with its text up to this many lines, then scroll.
.TP
.B \&.max_height(px: f32)
Makes the view grow with its text up to this height in px, then scroll. With \fBmax_lines\fR too, the smaller of the two applies.
.SH EVENTS
